<title>USA: PTI sees $2 million non-cash Q2 charge.</title>
<headline>PTI sees $2 million non-cash Q2 charge.</headline>
<dateline>HASTINGS-ON-THE HUDSON, N.Y. 1997-07-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>PTI Holding Inc said Wednesday it will take a non-cash charge of $2 million at the end of the second quarter in connection with the exercise of 402,390 of its redeemable public warrants.</p>
<p>The deal netted the company $3,017,925 before legal and accounting fees, which it said would be used to pay for certain acquisitions without the need for more debt.</p>
<p>PTI makes licensed brand name and private label products, including bicycle helmets, safety gear and other accessories for biking, in-line skating, skateboarding and other extreme sports.</p>
